  The idea of keeping things organized and shared is not new to most people that had overbearing parents. Personally, I found filmmaking the hardest projects to keep in good organization with multiple people working on the same files at the same time. Since they are always collaborative, and each participant has structured departments under them, open workspaces that are uniformly organized make sure things mesh well. Like ingesting footage, if the file structure isn't the same, then the work takes much longer to reproduce or even use since all that work has to be redone. Same, so the reading said, goes for research. I was actually under the impression that things were not this hard for researchers still, meaning the advent of the internet was for the very things that Munafò, M., Nosek, B., Bishop, D. et al. (2017) were trying to get across: we have to share to know where we are.
